 its inception in the late 1960s, including the types of research questions and methods that the study of Asians &amp; Pacific Islander peoples in the U.S. as well as politics and historical relations in the Asia/Pacific region have to offer. In this course, we will pay particular attention to the role of culture and its production in documenting histories, formulating critical practices, and galvanizing political efforts. Topics and themes include: war &amp; empire; queer &amp; feminist lives and histories; refugee, adoptees, transnational families, and other forms of kinship &amp; belonging; anti-Asian violence; settler colonialism and postcolonial critique.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "(CA-AS)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": null}, {"strm": 2727, "crseId": 357919, "crseOfferNbr": 2, "subject": "AAS", "catalogNbr": "2620", "titleShort": "Intro to Asian Am Lit", "titleLong": "Introduction to Asian American Literature", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9224, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:40AM", "timeEnd": "12:55PM", "startDt": "01/22/2019", "endDt": "05/07/2019", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "ssw6", "firstName": "Sunn", "middleName": "Shelley", "lastName": "Wong"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Statler Hall 341", "bldgDescr": "Statler Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "STL341", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": 